        "text": "#### **[8] Anthropic signs $35B cloud infrastructure deal with Nvidia-backed Lambda**\n* **What is confirmed:** *The Wall Street Journal* (corroborated by Bloomberg and Reuters) reported on August 31, 2026, that Anthropic signed a multi-year cloud computing agreement worth ~$35 billion with Nvidia-backed cloud provider Lambda"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0,
        1,
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 460,
        "endIndex": 620,
        "text": "Under the arrangement, Lambda will deploy Nvidia GPUs inside a 1-gigawatt Texas data center campus in Nueces County built by Hut 8, where Nvidia holds the lease"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        3,
        4,
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 622,
        "endIndex": 837,
        "text": "* **Important caveats:** The deal is reported via anonymous sources close to the negotiations; Anthropic, Nvidia, Lambda, and Hut 8 did not issue formal on-the-record statements confirming the exact contract figures"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        1,
        5
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 883,
        "endIndex": 937,
        "text": "** A major, widely corroborated AI infrastructure deal"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0,
        1,
        6
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 945,
        "endIndex": 1389,
        "text": "#### **[15] & [19] FTC and 22 US states sue Amazon over Sponsored Ads pricing; Amazon disputes claims**\n* **What is confirmed:** On August 31, 2026, the US Federal Trade Commission (FTC) and 22 state attorneys general filed a lawsuit in federal court against Amazon, alleging the company secretly manipulated its Sponsored Products ad auctions with undisclosed reserve prices, overcharging 1.2 million advertisers by over $20 billion since 2019"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        7,
        8
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1391,
        "endIndex": 1620,
        "text": "Amazon published an official response on *About Amazon*, arguing its auction model prioritizes ad relevancy, reduced average winning bids by 50% between 2019 and 2025, and that the FTC presented no evidence of consumer price harm"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        9,
        10
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1694,
        "endIndex": 1793,
        "text": "*\n* **Important caveats:** The lawsuit represents regulatory claims that will be litigated in court"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        10,
        8
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1839,
        "endIndex": 1902,
        "text": "** High-impact regulatory action and official corporate defense"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        9,
        8
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1910,
        "endIndex": 2146,
        "text": "#### **[11] Apple submits forensic laptop evidence in trade-secrets lawsuit against OpenAI**\n* **What is confirmed:** Apple filed court documents in California federal court on August 31, 2026, seeking expedited discovery against OpenAI"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        11,
        12
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2148,
        "endIndex": 2468,
        "text": "Apple stated that forensic examination of a work MacBook returned by former engineer Chang Liu revealed he downloaded a confidential power-converter circuit schematic, ran LTspice simulations with an AI agent at OpenAI in March 2026, and instructed a colleague to destroy evidence after learning of Apple's investigation"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        11,
        13,
        14
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2470,
        "endIndex": 2637,
        "text": "* **Important caveats:** These details are allegations made in legal briefs by Apple; OpenAI has previously denied trade-secret theft and sought to dismiss the lawsuit"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        11,
        14,
        12
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
